## Invoice Header Row Requirements

The `Invoice` row identifies the invoice-level record.

| Coupa CSV Field | Required? | What to Populate |
|---|---:|---|
| `Invoice` | Row type | Use this to identify the row as an invoice header. |
| `Invoice Number` | Yes | Invoice number from the vendor invoice. |
| `Invoice Date` | Yes | Date on the invoice. |
| `Supplier Name` or `Supplier Number` | Needed for lookup | Prefer `Supplier Number` if Upbound has stable Coupa vendor IDs. |
| `Line Level Taxation` | Yes | Boolean. For contractor invoices, default to `false` unless line-level tax is explicitly needed. |
| `Chart of Accounts` | Yes | Upbound's Coupa chart of accounts name or code. |
| `Local Currency Net` | Yes | Net invoice amount before tax. |
| `Taxes In Origin Country Currency` | Yes | Tax amount. For most contractor invoices, default to `0.00` if no tax exists. |
| `Local Currency Gross` | Yes | Total invoice amount including tax. |

### Recommended Header Defaults

| Field | MVP Default / Rule |
|---|---|
| `Status` | Use the value required by Upbound's Coupa process, such as `draft`, `new`, or `pending_approval`. |
| `Submit For Approval?` | Default to `no`. |
| `Currency` | Default to `USD` unless extracted invoice currency says otherwise. |
| `Requester Email` | Manager/requester email from internal mapping. |
| `Requester Name` | Manager/requester name from internal mapping. |
| `Payment Terms` | Pull from supplier master or leave blank if Coupa applies default supplier terms. |
| `Supplier Note` | Use for automation notes, Clarity match status, or exception summary. |
| `Attachment 1` | Leave blank for MVP. PDF/S3 support comes later. |

---

## Invoice Line Row Requirements

The `Invoice Line` row identifies the service line being imported.

| Coupa CSV Field | Required? | What to Populate |
|---|---:|---|
| `Invoice Line` | Row type | Identifies the row as an invoice line. |
| `Invoice Number` | Yes | Same invoice number as the header. |
| `Supplier Name` or `Supplier Number` | Lookup | Same supplier as the header. |
| `Description` | Yes | Service description from invoice or generated text. |
| `Price` | Yes | Hourly rate if `Quantity` is hours, or total line amount if quantity is `1`. |
| `Unit of Measure` | Yes | Must already exist in Coupa. Examples: `HOUR`, `EA`. |

### Recommended Invoice Line Fields for Contractor Invoices

| Coupa CSV Field | Why It Matters |
|---|---|
| `Line Number` | Needed to connect allocations and taxes to the line. |
| `Quantity` | Contractor hours from invoice. |
| `Price` | Hourly rate if quantity is hours; line total if quantity is 1. |
| `Category` | Example: `Contractor Services` or `Professional Services`. |
| `PO Number` | Include if invoices are PO-backed. |
| `PO Line Number` | Required if using PO matching and not using supplier part number. |
| `Account Code` | Leave blank. |
| `Account Segment 1-20` | Use these if Coupa expects segmented accounting fields. |
| `Budget Period Name` | Use if Coupa budget validation is enabled. |
| `Billing Notes` | Use for Clarity match notes. |

