## Optional Account Allocation Rows

Use `Account Allocation` rows only if one invoice line needs to be split across multiple projects, departments, budgets, cost centers, or account codes.

| Coupa CSV Field | What to Populate |
|---|---|
| `Account Allocation` | Row type for allocation. |
| `Invoice Number` | Parent invoice number. |
| `Invoice Line Number` | Parent invoice line number. |
| `Amount` | Dollar amount allocated to this account. |
| `Percent` | Percent allocated to this account. Use either amount or percent depending on Coupa setup. |
| `Account Code` | Full account code if available. |
| `Account Segment 1` | Company code. Company code id determined based on company the contractor works for. The company for each project is in the file "Company_by_Project" under the coloumn p labeled "line of business". If the company is RAC then company code = `5`, if company is ACIMA then company code = `67` |
| `Account Segment 2` | Cost Center. If RAC then = `H0003`, If ACIMA then = `AC000` |
| `Account Segment 3` | CAPEX or OPEX code. If CAPEX then code = `246010`, If OPEX then code = `667070` |
| `Account Segment 4` | Segment value configured by Upbound/Coupa. |
| `Budget Period Name` | Budget period, if required. |

