## Tax Fields

For most contractor invoices, taxes may be zero, but Coupa still requires certain header totals.

### Header-Level Tax Fields

| Coupa CSV Field | Use |
|---|---|
| `Tax Amount` | Header tax amount. |
| `Tax Rate` | Tax percentage. |
| `Tax Code` | Must exist in Coupa if used. |
| `Tax Rate Type` | Must exist in Coupa if used. |
| `Taxes In Origin Country Currency` | Required local/origin tax amount. |

### Line-Level Tax Fields

Only populate these if `Line Level Taxation = true`.

| Coupa CSV Field | Use |
|---|---|
| `Line Tax Amount` | Tax amount on the line. |
| `Line Tax Rate` | Tax rate on the line. |
| `Line Tax Code` | Must match an existing Coupa tax code. |
| `Line Tax Rate Type` | Coupa tax rate type. |
| `Line Tax Location` | Tax jurisdiction/location. |
| `Line Tax Description` | Tax description. |

### MVP Tax Rule

For the MVP contractor invoice workflow:

- Set `Line Level Taxation` to `false` by default.
- Set `Taxes In Origin Country Currency` to `0.00` when no tax is present.
- Set `Local Currency Net` equal to `Local Currency Gross` when tax is `0.00`.
- Do not generate line-level tax fields unless the invoice explicitly includes line-level tax and Coupa requires it.

